From 7e274a28639da218079084a3378adc33e9822fca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:08:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fig. 2: labels inside the schematics, tighter layout,
 wave-bounded bars in (f)

Labels (a)-(d) and the Herriott scale bar sit inside the schematics on
semi-transparent white boxes; the Herriott cells are drawn mirrored top
to bottom (same simulation): port at the bottom left. The CMPCs shrink
to the height of the stacked Herriott views, the rows sit closer and the
default size is 16.8 x 8.5 cm (21 cm preset: 10.4 cm).

Panel (f) shows wave-bounded bars by default: per layout, angle =
max(ray value, 0.98 x no dither) and both = max(ray value, 0.98 x
wavelength only), since a +-2 mrad tilt of the 40 um launch stays inside
the beam divergence; black marks give the ray-optics medians. The rail
selects wave+ray, wave only or ray only (the earlier figure); the
ensemble table and the settings file carry the wave-bounded values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NLfEqncaEw1RGMDLUGdFgb
